## Project Overview

This project demonstrates the implementation of OSPF (Open Shortest Path First) in a multi-router enterprise network using GNS3.

The network consists of four routers connected in a ring topology and four PCs connected to separate LANs. OSPF dynamically exchanges routing information between routers, allowing full connectivity across all networks.


Built a four-router enterprise network using OSPF Area 0.

Implemented:
- Dynamic Routing
- OSPF Neighbor Relationships
- Route Advertisement
- Router IDs
- End-to-End Connectivity
- Network Failover Testing

Tools:
- GNS3
- Cisco IOS
- VPCS

